# Local Engineering Rules

## Verification Before Handoff
- Both agents run the project's verification task before handoff and fix any
  failures.
- "Run unit tests" is ambiguous in a Multiplatform build, because every target
  has its own test task. Discover this project's gate once with
  `./gradlew tasks --group verification` and use the aggregate task it exposes.
  Do not assume a task name.
- Report which targets actually ran. A green `testDebugUnitTest` is evidence
  about Android only, and this project also ships iOS.

## Tool Order
- The cleaner runs `kover`, then `crap4kotlin`, then `dry4kotlin`, then
  `detekt`, then `mutate4kotlin`.
- `crap4kotlin` reads the Kover XML report and does not run tests itself, so
  `kover` has to run first or it has nothing to score.
- Mutation runs last. It is the slowest tool by a wide margin, and running it
  before the cheaper tools have settled the code means mutating code that is
  about to change.
